Contents of https://docs.rs/android_logger/0.15.1/android_logger/:
# Crate android\_logger 

[Source](../src/android_logger/lib.rs.html#8-239) 

Expand description

A logger which writes to android output.

### [§](#example)Example

```
#[macro_use] extern crate log;
extern crate android_logger;

use log::LevelFilter;
use android_logger::Config;

/// Android code may not have obvious "main", this is just an example.
fn main() {
    android_logger::init_once(
        Config::default().with_max_level(LevelFilter::Trace),
    );

    debug!("this is a debug {}", "message");
    error!("this is printed by default");
}
```

### [§](#example-with-module-path-filter)Example with module path filter

It is possible to limit log messages to output from a specific crate, and override the logcat tag name (by default, the crate name is used):

```
#[macro_use] extern crate log;
extern crate android_logger;

use log::LevelFilter;
use android_logger::{Config,FilterBuilder};

fn main() {
    android_logger::init_once(
        Config::default()
            .with_max_level(LevelFilter::Trace)
            .with_tag("mytag")
